  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\n```\r\n500: {\"errcode\":\"M_UNKNOWN\",\"error\":\"Internal server error\"}\r\nCouldn't find room.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis was the response returned when I tried to run `GetUserProfile.py` from `Matrix Client-server SDK for Python 2 and 3`\r\n\r\nThen I checked the server logs in that, I found that my home server was not correctly set up, it throwing `DNS Lookup failed`. But, also, in the `synapse/handlers/profile.py` file, in function `get_avatar_url()`, the result was throwing the error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nFile \"synapse/handlers/profile.py\", line 178, in get_avatar_url\r\n    defer.returnValue(result[\"avatar_url\"])\r\nexceptions.UnboundLocalError: local variable 'result' referenced before assignment\r\n```\r\nAnd that is expected too. As the query failed, the control passed over to `except` leaving the value of `result` uninitialized.",
